# VELORA Admin Website — environment variables
#
# These point at the SAME Supabase project the VELORA mobile app already
# uses (one shared backend — see README "Architecture"). Copy this file to
# .env.local and fill in real values from the Supabase dashboard
# (Project Settings -> API). Never commit .env.local.
#
# Both values below are safe to expose to the browser (that's what
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means in Next.js) — they are the same publishable/anon key
# already shipped inside the VELORA mobile app. Admin authorization is NOT
# based on possessing this key; it is enforced server-side by RLS via the
# admin_users table / is_admin() function (see supabase/migrations).
#
# Do NOT add a SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY here. Phase 1 of the admin website
# needs no service-role access at all — every read goes through the
# signed-in admin's own session plus the new admin-scoped RLS policies. If a
# future phase genuinely needs service-role access (e.g. a server-only
# action Supabase can't otherwise express), it must be added as a
# server-only env var (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix) and used only inside a
# server-side route handler — never bundled into client code.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
